Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:02:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Recognize unframed pointer tail calls before zero trap
 padding

Accept paired pointer loads and recognize a padded tail only for contiguous straight-line thunks that preserve SP, FP and LR. Keep rejecting unproven control flow, frame changes and pointer clobbers. Moving Out 2 1.3.315 rewrites successfully; Cuphead runtime outputs remain byte-identical.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#888
Reason: Rewrite proven unframed pointer tails with zero trap padding instead of rejecting them as jump tables.
Issue: seedds/nxnative#888
